WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.540
One, plus two, plus three,
all the way up to one hundred.

2
00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:06.360
A stopwatch starts.

3
00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:09.660
Most people begin adding,
one number at a time.

4
00:00:09.710 --> 00:00:13.660
But one pupil writes down the
total after just a few seconds.

5
00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:14.560
How?

6
00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:15.800
Are they just quick?

7
00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:18.260
Or could you take a
hundred times a hundred,

8
00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:19.780
then halve it?

9
00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.890
In this mission, you'll
meet arithmetic sequences,

10
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:26.240
which change by the same
common difference each time.

11
00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:31.050
You'll find any term of a sequence, then
prove a formula for the sum of an arithmetic

12
00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:31.990
series.

13
00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:36.200
And you'll write long sums
compactly, with sigma notation.

14
00:00:36.250 --> 00:00:41.160
Your mission: add every whole number
from one to one hundred in seconds,

15
00:00:41.210 --> 00:00:42.450
and explain how.
